# SWI-Prolog with Elixir

## Start here

Open [Getting started](01_basic.livemd) in Livebook. Run setup in the default
Standalone runtime, then work through the cells in order. The first run needs
internet to fetch dependencies and the SWI runtime. After setup, the examples
run locally.

The lessons install SWI Elixir 0.1.2 from Hex. Setup needs a published bundle for
your platform or a local archive. See the
[build guide](https://github.com/davfuenmayor/swi_elixir/blob/main/MULTIPLATFORM.md).

Read the question before running its cell, then change one input and try again.
The lesson programs, queries and data are in the cells. The prover and learner
notebooks include their engines in Setup.

## Chapters

| Notebook | Subject |
| --- | --- |
| [01 · Getting started](01_basic.livemd) | Queries, bindings and loading code |
| [02 · Proof search](02_provers.livemd) | Test whether a conclusion follows from assumptions |
| [03 · Constraint search](03_search.livemd) | N-queens and lazy search |
| [04 · Port and NIF](04_backends.livemd) | Timing, timeouts and crash recovery |
| [05 · Metagol](05_metagol.livemd) | Learn rules, recursion and list transformations |
| [06 · Aleph](06_aleph.livemd) | Learn a classifier and spot overfitting |

Run a lesson's final close cell before starting its session again. Restart
the runtime to clear embedded SWI state.
